  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Life is Strange: Double Exposure",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/6829/450x258/life-is-strange-double-exposure-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1793887200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/6829-buy-life-is-strange-double-exposure-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Al1X1RO",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/2093216-1722852977.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "The story is so far pretty nice, not on the level of the previous games but nice enough. While im fine with how the game is, i feel like this one in particular is forcing the lgbt stuff a lot down the players throat on every occasion it gets. Previous games were fine, couldnt complain but this one is too much, but not enough to turn me away for now at least.\n\n\n\nAside from that, the game has terrible optimization. I started it on PS5 but i lost interest, tho i must say it looked and ran pretty badly. Worse on PC. While i can run to a certain extent newer games, this one is horrendous something between 30 and 60fps depending on area and whether there are people in it or not."
    },
    {
      "game": "ARC Raiders",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/10142/450x258/arc-raiders-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1793887200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/10142-buy-arc-raiders-pc-steam/",
      "user": "PK3K",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "The game had potential, then it went to trash almost right away. Rampant cheating and extract camping. Sometimes you'd see 3 rats each jorking it in their own corner. Free kits are abysmal since you dont need nothing else to PVP, therefore your loadout is obsolote. Any and all . If you dont like PVP and decide on the PVE variant, there will be people sabotaging you or stealing the loot you fight for with the NPC robots. If you arent buying this specifically for its mediocre PVP mechanics. AVOID AT ALL COSTS."
    },
    {
      "game": "Runaway, A Road Adventure",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/8727/450x258/runaway-a-road-adventure-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1793887200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/8727-buy-runaway-a-road-adventure-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "SambaL",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/27742514-1746025891.jpg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "As a huge fan of basically any Lucas Arts era and Double fine remastered point & click adventure games for their humor and animation, the Runaway series made me loose hope in the genre. Terrible, just terrible."
    },
    {
      "game": "Eriksholm: The Stolen Dream",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/19764/450x258/eriksholm-the-stolen-dream-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1793887200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/19764-buy-eriksholm-the-stolen-dream-pc-steam/",
      "user": "SambaL",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/27742514-1746025891.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Only played the demo on Steam, which is pretty substantial by the way, and as far as I'm concerned this is a real gem. Not only does it look phenomenal, both in cutscenes and in game. It reminded me of the Commandos games from back in the day and how the photorealistic environments blew me away back then. The gameplay reminded me of it as well in a way, though it is less strategic based and more focussed on sneaking your way past guards across stunning setpieces to reach the end of a level.\n\n\n\nThere is a lot of optional collectables to read through but I really didn't mind as the setting and the story are quite interesting. \n\n\n\nA game I can strongly recommend."
    }
  ],
